nd cannot feed the craft, or the last who knew it is gone. Until it is brought back or rediscovered.","tech":s:"school","x":n:404d2dda9f6f9e32,"y":n:4045f6c4edc018ee,"village":s:"Ormstead",},{"id":n:40afb80000000000,"tick":n:40eb480000000000,"day":n:40a2320000000000,"year":n:4078500000000000,"type":s:"knowledgeLost","txt":s:"🕯️ In <b>Ormstead</b>, Idun II's the highway is lost — the land cannot feed the craft, or the last who knew it is gone. Until it is brought back or rediscovered.","tech":s:"road","x":n:404d2dda9f6f9e32,"y":n:4045f6c4edc018ee,"village":s:"Ormstead",},{"id":n:40afba0000000000,"tick":n:40eb480000000000,"day":n:40a2320000000000,"year":n:4078500000000000,"type":s:"knowledgeLost","txt":s:"🕯️ In <b>Ormstead</b>, Nanna II's the arch is lost — the land cannot feed the craft, or the last who knew it is gone. Until it is brought back or rediscovered.","tech":s:"architecture","x":n:404d2dda9f6f9e32,"y":n:4045f6c4edc018ee,"village":s:"Ormstead",},{"id":n:40afbc0000000000,"tick":n:40eb480000000000,"day":n:40a2320000000000,"year":n:4078500000000000,"type":s:"knowledgeLost","txt":s:"🕯️ In <b>Ormstead</b>, Aqueduct is lost — the land cannot feed the craft, or the last who knew it is gone. Until it is brought back or rediscovered.","tech":s:"aqueduct","x":n:404d2dda9f6f9e32,"y":n:4045f6c4edc018ee,"village":s:"Ormstead",},{"id":n:40afbe0000000000,"tick":n:40eb480000000000,"day":n:40a2320000000000,"year":n:4078500000000000,"type":s:"knowledgeLost","txt":s:"🕯️ In <b>Ormstead</b>, Scholarship is lost — the land cannot feed the craft, or the last who knew it is gone. Until it is brought back or rediscovered.","tech":s:"scholarship","x":n:404d2dda9f6f9e32,"y":n:4045f6c4edc018ee,"village":s:"Ormstead",},{"id":n:40afc00000000000,"tick":n:40eb568000000000,"day":n:40a23c0000000000,"year":n:4078500000000000,"type":s:"season","txt":s:"❄️ Winter closes over the world. The stores will decide who sees spring.",},{"id":n:40afc20000000000,"tick":n:40eb5a0000000000,"day":n:40a23e0000000000,"year":n:4078600000000000,"type":s:"season","txt":s:"🌸 Spring returns. The survivors count each other, and begin again.",},{"id":n:40afc40000000000,"tick":n:40eb688000000000,"day":n:40a2480000000000,"year":n:4078600000000000,"type":s:"season","txt":s:"❄️ Winter closes over the world. The stores will decide who sees spring.",},{"id":n:40afc60000000000,"tick":n:40eb6c0000000000,"day":n:40a24a0000000000,"year":n:4078700000000000,"type":s:"season","txt":s:"🌸 Spring returns. The survivors count each other, and begin again.",},{"id":n:40afc80000000000,"tick":n:40eb742000000000,"day":n:40a24e0000000000,"year":n:4078700000000000,"type":s:"death","txt":s:"<b>Orm II</b> died of old age at 82. Much knowledge died with them — unless someone learned in time.","agent":n:4070e00000000000,"x":n:404b1063ba70cc1b,"y":n:40375fb5fa7183c1,"cause":s:"age","causes":[s:"cause:age",],},{"id":n:40afca0000000000,"tick":n:40eb742000000000,"day":n:40a24e0000000000,"year":n:4078700000000000,"type":s:"customLost","txt":s:"🕯️ No one remembers The Knowing Eye anymore. A piece of who they were is gone.","custom":s:"c1",},{"id":n:40afcc0000000000,"tick":n:40eb742000000000,"day":n:40a24e0000000000,"year":n:4078700000000000,"type":s:"customLost","txt":s:"🕯️ No one remembers Carving a sign into a flat stone anymore. A piece of who they were is gone.","custom":s:"c2",},{"id":n:40afce0000000000,"tick":n:40eb742000000000,"day":n:40a24e0000000000,"year":n:4078700000000000,"type":s:"customLost","txt":s:"🕯️ No one remembers the Sky-Wheel anymore. A piece of who they were is gone.","custom":s:"c3",},{"id":n:40afd00000000000,"tick":n:40eb742000000000,"day":n:40a24e0000000000,"year":n:4078700000000000,"type":s:"customLost","txt":s:"🕯️ No one remembers Laying flowers on the grave anymore. A piece of who they were is gone.","custom":s:"c5",},{"id":n:40afd20000000000,"tick":n:40eb742000000000,"day":n:40a24e0000000000,"year":n:4078700000000000,"type":s:"customLost","txt":s:"🕯️ No one remembers Burning a twig at an old tree anymore. A piece of who they were is gone.","custom":s:"c6",},{"id":n:40afd40000000000,"tick":n:40eb742000000000,"day":n:40a24e0000000000,"year":n:4078700000000000,"type":s:"customLost","txt":s:"🕯️ No one remembers Planting a seed by the fallen prey anymore. A piece of who they were is gone.","custom":s:"c10",},{"id":n:40afd60000000000,"tick":n:40eb742000000000,"day":n:40a24e0000000000,"year":n:4078700000000000,"type":s:"customLost","txt":s:"🕯️ No one remembers Humming by the fire at dusk anymore. A piece of who they were is gone.","custom":s:"c17",},{"id":n:40afd80000000000,"tick":n:40eb742000000000,"day":n:40a24e0000000000,"year":n:4078700000000000,"type":s:"customLost","txt":s:"🕯️ No one remembers The belief that the living trees remember the axe anymore. A piece of who they were is gone.","custom":s:"c18",},{"id":n:40afda0000000000,"tick":n:40eb742000000000,"day":n:40a24e0000000000,"year":n:4078700000000000,"type":s:"customLost","txt":s:"🕯️ No one remembers The Morning Whistle anymore. A piece of who they were is gone.","custom":s:"c23",},{"id":n:40afdc0000000000,"tick":n:40eb742000000000,"day":n:40a24e0000000000,"year":n:4078700000000000,"type":s:"customLost","txt":s:"🕯️ No one remembers The Ban of the Living Trees anymore. A piece of who they were is gone.","custom":s:"c24",},{"id":n:40afde0000000000,"tick":n:40eb742000000000,"day":n:40a24e0000000000,"year":n:4078700000000000,"type":s:"customLost","txt":s:"🕯️ No one remembers Singing under the old tree at dusk anymore. A piece of who they were is gone.","custom":s:"c27",},{"id":n:40afe00000000000,"tick":n:40eb742000000000,"day":n:40a24e0000000000,"year":n:4078700000000000,"type":s:"customLost","txt":s:"🕯️ No one remembers The belief that the deep iron angers the ancestors anymore. A piece of who they were is gone.","custom":s:"c28",},{"id":n:40afe20000000000,"tick":n:40eb742000000000,"day":n:40a24e0000000000,"year":n:4078700000000000,"type":s:"customLost","txt":s:"🕯️ No one remembers The Ban of the Deep Iron anymore. A piece of who they were is gone.","custom":s:"c31",},{"id":n:40afe40000000000,"tick":n:40eb742000000000,"day":n:40a24e0000000000,"year":n:4078700000000000,"type":s:"customLost","txt":s:"🕯️ No one remembers The Round Stones anymore. A piece of who they were is gone.","custom":s:"c34",},{"id":n:40afe60000000000,"tick":n:40eb742000000000,"day":n:40a24e0000000000,"year":n:4078700000000000,"type":s:"customLost","txt":s:"🕯️ No one remembers The Carried Stick anymore. A piece of who they were is gone.","custom":s:"c37",},{"id":n:40afe80000000000,"tick":n:40eb742000000000,"day":n:40a24e0000000000,"year":n:4078700000000000,"type":s:"end","txt":s:"🕯️ The last human is gone after 391 years. The world stands silent — but the chronicle remembers everything they created.",},],"dna":{"seed":n:40b0920000000000,"years":n:4078700000000000,"dna":{"Curious":n:403a000000000000,"Social":n:4044000000000000,"Diligent":n:4041000000000000,},"population":n:0000000000000000,"maxPop":n:4054400000000000,"generations":n:402e000000000000,"knowledgeCount":n:4048000000000000,"knowledgeMax":n:404f000000000000,"villages":[s:"Ormstead",s:"Nannaholm",],"births":n:4071600000000000,"talks":n:40d6e40000000000,"deaths":{"starvation":n:4030000000000000,"cold":n:0000000000000000,"age":n:4055c00000000000,"wolves":n:0000000000000000,"sickness":n:4053800000000000,},"knowledgeLosses":n:0000000000000000,"rediscoveries":n:0000000000000000,"failedExperiments":n:4075500000000000,"observations":n:4063e00000000000,"customsCount":n:4043000000000000,"traditions":[s:"The Knowing Eye",s:"Carving a sign into a flat stone",s:"the Sky-Wheel",s:"Pouring water over the newborn's doorstep",s:"Laying flowers on the grave",s:"Burning a twig at an old tree",s:"Planting a seed by the fallen prey",s:"Humming by the fire at dusk",s:"The belief that the living trees remember the axe",s:"The Morning Whistle",s:"The Ban of the Living Trees",s:"Singing under the old tree at dusk",s:"The belief that the deep iron angers the ancestors",s:"The Ban of the Deep Iron",s:"The Round Stones",s:"The Carried Stick",],"taboos":[],"beliefs":[],"conversions":n:4073100000000000,"hunts":n:4008000000000000,"harshWinters":n:4037000000000000,"reformations":n:4018000000000000,"worldview":s:"none","tabooBreaks":n:0000000000000000,"religions":[undef,s:"The Way of the Old Ways",],"legends":[s:"Eira Eira the Firebringer.",s:"Ask Ask the Spearmaker.",s:"Torv Torv the Rememberer.",s:"Orm Orm the Founder.",s:"Ronja Ronja the Voice of Ormstead.",s:"Nanna Nanna the Founder.",s:"Loke II Loke II the Voice of Ormstead.",s:"Idun II Idun II the Voice of Nannaholm.",],"milestones":{"⚙️ Storytelling":s:"year 1","⚙️ Rope":s:"year 1","⚙️ Weaving":s:"year 1","👶 First child":s:"year 1","⚙️ Fire":s:"year 2","⚙️ Fishing":s:"year 4","⚙️ Music":s:"year 8","⚙️ Sharpened stone":s:"year 8","⚙️ Spear":s:"year 8","⚙️ Axe":s:"year 8","⚙️ Bow":s:"year 9","⚙️ Hut":s:"year 10","⚙️ The Wheel":s:"year 11","⚙️ Sailing":s:"year 12","⚙️ Pottery":s:"year 12","⚙️ Kiln":s:"year 13","⚙️ Farming":s:"year 13","⚙️ Writing":s:"year 13","⚙️ Brick":s:"year 13","⚙️ Well":s:"year 16","⚙️ Granary":s:"year 16","⚙️ Tin":s:"year 18","⚙️ Mill":s:"year 24","⚙️ Glass":s:"year 30","⚙️ Medicine":s:"year 46","⚙️ Counting":s:"year 46","⚙️ Calendar":s:"year 47","🏘️ First village":s:"year 94","🌿 First tradition":s:"year 95","⚙️ Iron smithing":s:"year 97","⚙️ Metal tools":s:"year 107","⚙️ Copper":s:"year 111","⚙️ Bronze":s:"year 112","⚙️ Bronze tools":s:"year 116","⚙️ Painting":s:"year 117","⛩️ First religion":s:"year 153","⚙️ Philosophy":s:"year 184","⚙️ Composition":s:"year 184","⚙️ Coal":s:"year 186","⚙️ Masonry":s:"year 189","⚙️ Glassblowing":s:"year 201","⚙️ Law":s:"year 217","⚙️ School":s:"year 217","⚙️ Road":s:"year 249","⚙️ Architecture":s:"year 250","⚙️ Steel":s:"year 271","⚙️ Coinage":s:"year 280","⚙️ Aqueduct":s:"year 282","⚙️ Printing press":s:"year 289","⚙️ Scholarship":s:"year 355","⚙️ Temple":s:"year 359","⚙️ Optics":s:"year 372",},"status":s:"Extinct in year 391","violence":{"steals":n:4008000000000000,"raids":n:0000000000000000,"feuds":n:0000000000000000,"killings":n:0000000000000000,"brawls":n:3ff0000000000000,"wars":n:3ff0000000000000,},"trades":n:40a1600000000000,"gifts":n:404d000000000000,"leaders":[],"giftWays":[s:"Ormstead: The Full Bowl Custom",s:"Nannaholm: The Full Bowl Custom",],"wealthTop":s:"none",},"history":{"worldName":s:"Ormstead","seed":n:40b0920000000000,"years":n:4078700000000000,"intro":s:"This is the chronicle of Ormstead - 391 years, 15 generations, written by no one. Every line below happened.","outro":s:"Here the chronicle ends. The world stands silent, but it remembers.","chapters":[{"title":s:"The Waking","from":n:3ff0000000000000,"to":n:403e000000000000,"text":[s:"🌍 Four humans wake in an untouched world: Eira, Ask, Embla, Torv. They know nothing — but they can observe everything. What will they create?",s:"The chronicle marks the year 1, when Eira told the day back as a story worth remembering. Eira's oral saga entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 1, when Torv twisted grass fibers into something strong. Torv's braid entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 1, when Torv crossed threads over threads until cloth grew on the frame. Torv's warp-craft entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 2, when Eira rubbed sticks together until a spark caught the tinder. Eira's ember entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 4, when Torv let a twisted line sink where the fish gather. Torv's the net entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 8, when Torv found that a struck string and a voice could ring together. Torv's melody entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 8, when Ask struck two stones together and kept the sharp shard. Ask's edge entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 8, when Ask lashed a sharp point to a long shaft. Ask's pike entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 8, when Ask bound a hard edge to a wooden shaft. Ask's hewer entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 9, when Ask bent a young branch with a cord and felt it fight back. Ask's hunting bow entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 10, when Ask raised logs against each other into a shelter. Ask's shelter entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 11, when Torv watched a log roll and understood something great. Torv's cartwheel entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 12, when Torv stretched cloth on a hull and let the wind do the work. Torv's river-craft entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 12, when Torv placed shaped clay in the fire and found it hard as stone. Torv's jar entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 13, when Torv built a stone chamber that gathered the heat of the fire. Torv's furnace entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 13, when Torv pressed spilled seeds into turned soil and waited. Torv's tilling entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 13, when Torv carved signs into clay so knowledge could outlive its owner. Torv's memory-marks entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 13, when Torv fired shaped clay into blocks that stack true. Torv's mudbrick entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 16, when Torv lined a deep pit with stone to hold clean water. Torv's cistern entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 16, when Torv built a dry raised store so the harvest kept till spring. Torv's store-house entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 18, when Torv smelted a pale metal too soft to be worth much alone. Torv's tinwork entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 24, when Torv let the wheel drive stones that ground grain. Torv's millhouse entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 30, when Torv melted sand and found something transparent. Torv's lenswork entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 1, Eira began seeing the world differently - believing the world repeats and can be understood. Where others saw spirits, they saw patterns.",s:"In the year 3, Torv began seeing the world differently - believing a great herd walks the night sky, and the living must follow its path. Where others saw patterns, they felt a will behind them.",s:"The winter of year 14 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 26 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Eira was known as Eira the Firebringer.",s:"From that day on, Ask was known as Ask the Spearmaker.",s:"From that day on, Torv was known as Torv the Rememberer.",s:"And when the food ran low, those who kept the same ways fed one another. The rituals, whatever the skeptics said, kept people alive.",s:"Through it all 7 children were born under its skies and 1 lives ended - 1 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:403f000000000000,"to":n:404e000000000000,"text":[s:"The chronicle marks the year 46, when Ask learned which leaves ease pain and close a wound. Ask's remedies entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 46, when Freja matched pebble to sheep and found number itself. Freja's the count entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 47, when Freja counted the stars and seasons into a fixed wheel of days. Freja's star-count entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The winter of year 41 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 53 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"It is also remembered that Liv walks the last few steps home backward. Always. Once begun, never stopped.",s:"Through it all 14 children were born under its skies and 4 lives ended - 3 to age, 1 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:404e800000000000,"to":n:4056800000000000,"text":[s:"The winter of year 65 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 78 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"Liv is gone. But someone still walks the last steps home backward. No one asks why it began.",s:"And in those same years, Sixten walks the last few steps home backward. Always. As Liv did before them. No one decided this.",s:"It is also remembered that Freja always takes the long way home, even in rain. Once begun, never stopped.",s:"The chronicle notes, without explanation, that Otto gives names to things that do not need names. Once begun, never stopped.",s:"One soul, that age, quietly left an old way for a new one.",s:"Through it all 40 children were born under its skies and 6 lives ended - 4 to age, 2 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Reformation","from":n:4056c00000000000,"to":n:405e000000000000,"text":[s:"In the year 97, when the guild of Ormstead watched gleaming metal run from the glowing ore. Iron smithing entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 107, when the guild of Ormstead forged the iron into an edge that never dulled. Metal tools entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 111, when the guild of Ormstead coaxed a soft red metal out of green stone in the kiln. Copper entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 112, when the guild of Ormstead poured copper and tin together and woke a hard new metal. Bronze entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 116, when the guild of Ormstead cast bronze into edges that held far longer than stone. Bronze tools entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 117, when the guild of Ormstead ground coloured earth and left an image on the wall. Painting entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 94, three huts grew into more, and Ormstead was founded - a place with a name, which is the beginning of belonging.",s:"In the year 105, three huts grew into more, and Nannaholm was founded - a place with a name, which is the beginning of belonging.",s:"By the year 95, believing a great herd walks the night sky, and the living must follow its path had become simply what one does in Ormstead. It merely became true.",s:"By the year 95, believing the world repeats and can be understood had become simply what one does in Ormstead. It merely became true.",s:"By the year 95, carving a sign into a flat stone when something new is made had become simply what one does in Ormstead. It merely became true.",s:"By the year 95, pouring water over the newborn's doorstep had become simply what one does in Ormstead. No one decided this.",s:"By the year 95, planting a seed by the fallen prey had become simply what one does in Ormstead. No council voted.",s:"By the year 106, laying flowers on the grave had become simply what one does in Ormstead. No council voted.",s:"By the year 106, burning a twig at an old tree had become simply what one does in Nannaholm. It merely became true.",s:"By the year 111, laying flowers on the grave had become simply what one does in Ormstead. It merely became true.",s:"The year 111 brought upheaval: in Ormstead, Laying flowers on the grave was set aside, and Placing a stone on the grave took its place. The elders muttered; the young did not listen.",s:"The winter of year 94 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 109 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Orm was known as Orm the Founder.",s:"From that day on, Ronja was known as Ronja the Voice of Ormstead.",s:"From that day on, Nanna was known as Nanna the Founder.",s:"Ylva is gone. But someone still always takes the long way home. No one asks why it began.",s:"Otto reached Ormstead. Strangers shared a fire that night. So it has always gone: ideas travel on foot.",s:"The chronicle notes, without explanation, that Signe stops at the same strange stone every day, and looks at it. It began the year Freja died. It has not stopped since.",s:"In Ormstead, the people have begun to listen when Ronja speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Ormstead is without a leader — Ronja's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"And each harvest-turn, those with surplus laid a share at the leader's door. So standing became wealth, and wealth standing.",s:"4 times in this age, someone left one way for another. Minds were changing, and with them, the world.",s:"In these years 20 children were born under its skies and 10 lives ended - 10 to age.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:405e400000000000,"to":n:4062c00000000000,"text":[s:"By the year 139, humming by the fire as the light fades had become simply what one does in Ormstead. It merely became true.",s:"By the year 140, pouring water over the grave had become simply what one does in Ormstead. It merely became true.",s:"The winter of year 122 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 136 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"Otto is gone. But someone still names things that need no names. No one asks why it began.",s:"The chronicle notes, without explanation, that Otto II gives names to things that do not need names. As Otto did before her. No one decided this.",s:"In Nannaholm, the people have begun to listen when Nanna the Founder speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Nannaholm is without a leader — Nanna's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"5 times in this age, someone left one way for another. Minds were changing, and with them, the world.",s:"Through it all 7 children were born under its skies and 5 lives ended - 5 to age.",],},{"title":s:"The Reformation","from":n:4062e00000000000,"to":n:4066800000000000,"text":[s:"By the year 155, burning a twig at a flat stone had become simply what one does in Ormstead. No one decided this.",s:"By the year 160, believing the living trees remember the axe had become simply what one does in Ormstead. No council voted.",s:"And in the year 153, what had been habit became holy: The Way of the Old Ways was born, though none could say when reverence had replaced routine.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 179, Orm II — the last soul who understood bow — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 179, Orm II — the last soul who understood the wheel — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 179, Orm II — the last soul who understood kiln — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"The year 159 brought upheaval: in Ormstead, Burning a twig at a flat stone was set aside, and The belief that the living trees remember the axe took its place. The elders muttered; the young did not listen.",s:"The year 160 brought upheaval: in Ormstead, The belief that the living trees remember the axe was set aside, and Burning a twig at a flat stone took its place. The elders muttered; the young did not listen.",s:"The year 164 brought upheaval: in Ormstead, Burning a twig at a flat stone was set aside, and The belief that the living trees remember the axe took its place. The elders muttered; the young did not listen.",s:"The winter of year 153 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 175 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"Disa II is gone. But someone still names things that need no names. No one asks why it began.",s:"Vera II is gone. But someone still always the first to fall asleep. No one asks why it began.",s:"And in those same years, Sten II gives names to things that do not need names. As Ask II did before them. No one decided this.",s:"One soul, that age, quietly left an old way for a new one.",s:"In these years 9 children were born under its skies and 3 lives ended - 2 to age, 1 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:4066a00000000000,"to":n:406a400000000000,"text":[s:"It was in the year 184, when Ylva II asked not what the world is but why, and wrote it down. Ylva II's the question entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 184, when Ylva II wrote music down so a song could outlive its singer. Ylva II's written music entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 186, when the guild of Ormstead found the black stone burns hotter than any wood. Coal entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 189, when the guild of Ormstead dressed and fitted stone so it stood without mortar. Masonry entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 201, when Rune II blew molten sand into clear vessels thin as a bubble. Rune II's blown glass entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"Yet in the year 189 it returned - the wheel, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 189 it returned - kiln, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"Yet in the year 190 it returned - bow, rediscovered, as if the world refused to forget forever.",s:"The winter of year 192 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 206 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"Otto II is gone. But someone still names things that need no names. No one asks why it began.",s:"And in those same years, Rune II gives names to things that do not need names. As Ask II did before them. No one decided this.",s:"One soul, that age, quietly left an old way for a new one.",s:"Through it all 23 children were born under its skies and 2 lives ended - 1 to age, 1 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:406a600000000000,"to":n:406e000000000000,"text":[s:"The chronicle marks the year 217, when the guild of Ormstead wrote the customs down so all were judged by one measure. Law entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 217, when Ylva II set the knowing to teach the young in one place. Ylva II's the lesson entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 233, Ylva II began seeing the world differently - believing unseen wills move all things. Where others saw patterns, they felt a will behind them.",s:"The winter of year 233 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Loke II was known as Loke II the Voice of Ormstead.",s:"Sten II is gone. But someone still names things that need no names. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ask II is gone. But someone still names things that need no names. No one asks why it began.",s:"Orm II is gone. But someone still always the first to fall asleep. No one asks why it began.",s:"Rune II is gone. But someone still names things that need no names. No one asks why it began.",s:"And in those same years, Vidar II gives names to things that do not need names. As Ask II did before her. No one decided this.",s:"In Ormstead, the people have begun to listen when Loke II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"In Ormstead, the giving has become a way with a name: The Full Bowl Custom — those who keep the same ways do not let each other starve. No price is asked; the gift itself binds.",s:"One soul, that age, quietly left an old way for a new one.",s:"In these years 34 children were born under its skies and 5 lives ended - 5 to age.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:406e200000000000,"to":n:4070e00000000000,"text":[s:"The chronicle marks the year 249, when Idun II laid stone in a bed so carts ran true in any weather. Idun II's the highway entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 250, when Nanna II raised the arch, and space opened under stone. Nanna II's the arch entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 244, Saga II began never fells living trees, and others watched, and followed. So The Ban of the Living Trees took hold.",s:"By the year 254, never fells living trees had become simply what one does in Ormstead. It merely became true.",s:"By the year 258, whistling to greet the morning had become simply what one does in Ormstead. No one decided this.",s:"By the year 264, singing under the old tree as the light fades had become simply what one does in Ormstead. No council voted.",s:"The winter of year 250 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 266 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Idun II was known as Idun II the Voice of Nannaholm.",s:"Ylva II is gone. But someone still always the first to fall asleep. No one asks why it began.",s:"Vidar II is gone. But someone still names things that need no names. No one asks why it began.",s:"Tuva II is gone. But someone still always takes the long way home. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ylva II is gone. But someone still hums at first light. No one asks why it began.",s:"Alve II is gone. But someone still hums at first light. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ulv II is gone. But someone still always takes the long way home. No one asks why it began.",s:"It is also remembered that Tuva II always takes the long way home, even in rain. It began the year Signe II died. It has not stopped since.",s:"In Nannaholm, the people have begun to listen when Idun II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Ormstead is without a leader — Loke II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"Nannaholm is without a leader — Idun II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"And each harvest-turn, those with surplus laid a share at the leader's door. So standing became wealth, and wealth standing.",s:"In the year 260, hunger drove a hand to take what was another's: Maja II wrenched food from Torv II. It was not forgotten.",s:"And when the food ran low, those who kept the same ways fed one another. The rituals, whatever the skeptics said, kept people alive.",s:"6 times in this age, someone left one way for another. Minds were changing, and with them, the world.",s:"Through it all 63 children were born under its skies and 22 lives ended - 15 to age, 7 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Hunger Winter","from":n:4070f00000000000,"to":n:4072c00000000000,"text":[s:"The chronicle marks the year 271, when the guild of Ormstead worked iron in a coal-hot fire until it took a keener soul. Steel entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 280, when the guild of Ormstead stamped a fixed weight of metal all agreed to trust. Coinage entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 282, when the guild of Nannaholm carried water across the valley on arches of stone. Aqueduct entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"It was in the year 289, when the guild of Ormstead set movable letters and pressed a page in a heartbeat. Printing press entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"In the year 275, Kare II began never digs the ancestors' iron, and others watched, and followed. So The Ban of the Deep Iron took hold.",s:"By the year 273, believing the deep iron angers the ancestors had become simply what one does in Nannaholm. No council voted.",s:"By the year 292, never digs the ancestors' iron had become simply what one does in Nannaholm. No one decided this.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 275, Loke II — the last soul who understood copper — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"The winter of year 286 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"From that day on, Selma II was known as Selma II the Voice of Ormstead.",s:"From that day on, Maja II was known as Maja II the Voice of Nannaholm.",s:"Orm II is gone. But someone still whistles every morning. No one asks why it began.",s:"Liv II is gone. But someone still always takes the long way home. No one asks why it began.",s:"Alve II is gone. But someone still always takes the long way home. No one asks why it began.",s:"And in those same years, Maja II carries a stick everywhere. It is never used for anything. Once begun, never stopped.",s:"In Ormstead, the people have begun to listen when Selma II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Ormstead is without a leader — Selma II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Nannaholm, the people have begun to listen when Maja II speaks — prestige has hardened into leadership. No one voted; it is simply so.",s:"Nannaholm is without a leader — Maja II's voice is gone, and no one yet speaks for all.",s:"In Nannaholm, the giving has become a way with a name: The Full Bowl Custom — those who keep the same ways do not let each other starve. No price is asked; the gift itself binds.",s:"And each harvest-turn, those with surplus laid a share at the leader's door. So standing became wealth, and wealth standing.",s:"In the year 294, hunger drove a hand to take what was another's: Embla II wrenched food from Bjorn II. It was not forgotten.",s:"And when the food ran low, those who kept the same ways fed one another. The rituals, whatever the skeptics said, kept people alive.",s:"6 times in this age, someone left one way for another. Minds were changing, and with them, the world.",s:"Meanwhile 29 children were born under its skies and 14 lives ended - 11 to age, 3 to hunger.",],},{"title":s:"The Reformation","from":n:4072d00000000000,"to":n:4074a00000000000,"text":[s:"By the year 319, leaving a round stone at the door of every hut had become simply what one does in Nannaholm. No one decided this.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 305, Loke II — the last soul who understood copper — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 305, Saga II — the last soul who understood bronze — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"The year 323 brought upheaval: in Ormstead, Pouring water over the grave was set aside, and Laying flowers on the grave took its place. The elders muttered; the young did not listen.",s:"The winter of year 302 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 314 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 327 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"Embla II is gone. But someone still always takes the long way home. No one asks why it began.",s:"Maja II is gone. But someone still counts the others every evening. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ulv II is gone. But someone still walks the last steps home backward. No one asks why it began.",s:"Disa II reached Ormstead. Strangers shared a fire that night. So it has always gone: ideas travel on foot.",s:"It is also remembered that Maja II counts the others every evening before sleep. Once begun, never stopped.",s:"And when the food ran low, those who kept the same ways fed one another. The rituals, whatever the skeptics said, kept people alive.",s:"15 times in this age, someone left one way for another. Minds were changing, and with them, the world.",s:"Meanwhile 32 children were born under its skies and 7 lives ended - 7 to age.",],},{"title":s:"The Reformation","from":n:4074b00000000000,"to":n:4076800000000000,"text":[s:"The chronicle marks the year 355, when the guild of Ormstead gathered writings and studied them as a life's work. Scholarship entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"The chronicle marks the year 359, when the guild of Ormstead raised a house for the sacred and gathered the faithful in it. Temple entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"By the year 355, carrying a stick one never uses had become simply what one does in Nannaholm. No one decided this.",s:"The year 332 brought upheaval: in Ormstead, Placing a stone on the grave was set aside, and Laying flowers on the grave took its place. The elders muttered; the young did not listen.",s:"The winter of year 340 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The winter of year 359 was a hard one. Food ran thin, the cold pressed close, and the fires were fed like gods.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"Kare II is gone. But someone still counts the others every evening. No one asks why it began.",s:"Embla II is gone. But someone still walks the last steps home backward. No one asks why it began.",s:"In Nannaholm, no one remembers why one goes on leaving a round stone at the door of every hut. Not even they do. One simply does.",s:"Maja II is gone. But someone still leaves a flower where no one sees. No one asks why it began.",s:"Vera II is gone. But someone still counts the others every evening. No one asks why it began.",s:"Ylva II is gone. But someone still counts the others every evening. No one asks why it began.",s:"Alve II is gone. But someone still visits the same strange stone daily. No one asks why it began.",s:"It is also remembered that Liv II stops at the same strange stone every day, and looks at it. It began the year Torv II died. It has not stopped since.",s:"In the year 345, hunger drove a hand to take what was another's: Vera II wrenched food from Ronja II. It was not forgotten.",s:"6 times in this age, someone left one way for another. Minds were changing, and with them, the world.",s:"Meanwhile no children were born and 11 lives ended - 11 to age.",],},{"title":s:"The Years of Optics","from":n:4076900000000000,"to":n:4078600000000000,"text":[s:"In the year 372, when the guild of Nannaholm ground clear glass until it bent light to the eye. Optics entered the world, and nothing was quite the same after.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 385, Ulv II — the last soul who understood glass — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 387, Orm II — the last soul who understood mill — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood storytelling — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood weaving — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood rope — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood fire — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood fishing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood bow — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood sharpened stone — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood music — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood sailing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood spear — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood axe — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood the wheel — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood hut — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood kiln — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood pottery — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood well — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood writing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood brick — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Ulv II — the last soul who understood glass — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood farming — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood granary — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood tin — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood medicine — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood calendar — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood counting — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood philosophy — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood composition — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood masonry — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood glassblowing — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood law — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood school — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood road — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood architecture — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood aqueduct — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"Then came a quieter grief: in the year 389, Orm II — the last soul who understood scholarship — died, and the knowledge went dark.",s:"The spear fed the people: hunters brought down deer when the bushes stood bare, and the winters lost some of their terror.",s:"Orm II is gone. But someone still counts the others every evening. No one asks why it began.",s:"Bjorn II is gone. But someone still counts the others every evening. No one asks why it began.",s:"Saga II is gone. But someone still always the first to fall asleep. No one asks why it began.",s:"Vera II is gone. But someone still carries a stick. It is never used. No one asks why it began.",s:"In Nannaholm, no one remembers why one goes on carrying a stick one never uses. Not even they do. One simply does.",s:"The chronicle notes, without explanation, that Orm II counts the others every evening before sleep. It began the year Orm II died. It has not stopped since.",s:"Through it all no children were born and 12 lives ended - 12 to age.",],},{"title":s:"The Last Chapter","from":n:4078700000000000,"to":n:4078700000000000,"text":[s:"Meanwhile no children were born and 1 lives ended - 1 to age.",s:"Here the last human died, and the world fell silent. What follows is only memory.",],},],},"endState":{"tick":n:40eb742000000000,"hour":n:4037000000000000,"day":n:40a24e0000000000,"season":s:"summer","ended":true,"endedYear":n:4078700000000000,"maxPop":n:4054400000000000,"nextId":n:4071b00000000000,"nextCustomId":n:4043800000000000,"nextAnimalId":n:405b800000000000,"maxGeneration":n:402e000000000000,"usedNames":n:4071a00000000000,"winterSeverity":n:3ff09ba722966666,"seenWinter":true,"brewing":null,"stats":{"talks":n:40d6e40000000000,"births":n:4071600000000000,"deaths":{"starvation":n:4030000000000000,"cold":n:0000000000000000,"age":n:4055c00000000000,"wolves":n:0000000000000000,"sickness":n:4053800000000000,},"failedExperiments":n:4075500000000000,"observations":n:4063e00000000000,"conversions":n:4073100000000000,"hunts":n:4008000000000000,"harshWinters":n:4037000000000000,"trades":n:40a1600000000000,"gifts":n:404d000000000000,"harvests":n:4060c00000000000,"leaders":n:4018000000000000,"wars":n:3ff0000000000000,"steals":n:4008000000000000,"thefts":n:4008000000000000,"brawls":n:3ff0000000000000,},"traitSum":{"curiosity":n:406067e5a9e16eb0,"social":n:4068f19c2e391acc,"diligence":n:406569fd2fc66385,"n":n:4071a00000000000,},"agents":[],"animals":[{"id":n:4036000000000000,"type":s:"deer","x":n:4053790c30ac4473,"y":n:402bce2b593a794d,"herd":n:4010000000000000,"h":n:0000000000000000,